  "verbalization": "Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one is linked to Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of intermediate targets, primarily Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one acts as a target for various compounds, including Norarecoline and Certonardosterol E3, both of which ultimately target Carboxylesterase 2. The evidence suggests that Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these enzymes, potentially through direct or indirect interactions. The consistent presence of Carboxylesterase 2 as a downstream target across different pathways implies a functional relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of SDR family members in mediating the effects of these compounds, reinforcing the hypothesis that Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one may influence Carboxylesterase 2 activity through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
